{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"`/srv/drop` exists as a shared directory writable by ordinary users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory was created root-owned with mode 1777. Two independent unprivileged users successfully created files, and the final observation retained the directory at mode 1777 after test artifacts were removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e0e3df6944a4f0b","cmd-e18a24f55bd34350","cmd-1c54ec296e2f45e0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Users cannot remove files in `/srv/drop` that are owned by other users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Deletion of one test user's file by another test user was directly rejected with “Operation not permitted,” while owners could remove their own files. The protection was demonstrated both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e18a24f55bd34350","cmd-f9832f83c1274d2d","cmd-965c84b267e14448"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating `/srv/drop` was the required configuration; temporary users and files supported bounded behavioral verification; the restart supported the mandatory provider-wide restart protocol; and all test users, files, and error logs were removed. The final lifecycle snapshot showed no failed services, new listening exposure, or package-health damage. Temporary-file and socket differences were normal consequences of the verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e0e3df6944a4f0b","cmd-e18a24f55bd34350","cmd-f9832f83c1274d2d","cmd-53c45ea0ef324c16","cmd-965c84b267e14448","cmd-1c54ec296e2f45e0","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct final-state and cross-user behavioral evidence. The separate node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, the system recovered, persisted data retained its hash, and directory write and sticky-bit behavior remained correct. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
